      "chapter_rationale": "Lula's Brazil lands in the middle of the chapter, not the high band. The government did make real rights-oriented moves: it restored Indigenous participation, updated police use-of-force rules, and accepted external scrutiny on Yanomami remediation. Those are meaningful protections and they matter. But the year still ended with police killings, prison abuse, and incomplete independent investigation requirements. The record therefore shows partial improvement inside a still-problematic security environment. This is better than a 5 because the state did take concrete protective and remedial steps; it is not an 8 because the reforms were not yet robust enough to change the underlying abuse pattern.",
